# Phase 10.31.1 — Retry Policy Preservation Hotfix

- Added configurable node retry policy controls in Create Workflow and Manage Workflows for tool, API, child workflow, and Temporal template nodes.
- Preserved `retryPolicy` and `timeoutMs` when loading and saving existing workflow graphs so visual/card edits no longer flatten seeded retry behavior.
- Added server-side normalization for workflow node retry policies and node timeout values.
- Added manual retry lineage offsets so node attempt counters continue from the previous run when a failed/canceled/terminated run is retried from Workflow History.
- Added retry policy and node timeout details to the visual workflow inspector.
- Added seed `00053__workflow_retry_policy_hotfix.sql` to restore macro ingestion retry/timeout defaults that were flattened by earlier graph saves.

# Phase 10.31 — Run Controls

- Added SkyServer workflow run control API endpoints for cancel, terminate, and retry from Workflow History.
- Cancel and terminate requests now call Temporal when a linked workflow execution exists, then update the SkyServer workflow ledger.
- Added safe local-ledger fallback when a Temporal execution is no longer available after local dev-server restarts.
- Active workflow node runs are finalized as CANCELED or TERMINATED during run-control cleanup, and pending human approvals are canceled.
- Failed, canceled, or terminated workflow runs can now be retried as a fresh Temporal-backed execution using the original saved input and retry lineage metadata.
- Added permission-aware Workflow History controls for Cancel run, Terminate, and Retry run.
- No DB migration required.

