- Reused the visual workflow graph on Workflow History as a read-only runtime overlay for the selected run.
- Added node-level runtime badges and styling for completed, running, pending approval, failed, terminated, skipped/not-run, and unknown node states.
- Added runtime metrics to the visual inspector, including attempts, duration, approval status, branch decision, output summary, and node error text.
- Highlighted condition branch decisions on the visual edge after the condition node when execution output records a selected branch.
- Kept the overlay observability-only: no DB migration, no executor/runtime changes, and no graph mutation from History.

## Phase 10.29.1 - Condition Branch Render Hotfix
- Fixed Admin-Web blank screen when adding or switching a node to `CONDITION` in Manage Workflows.
- Passed the current workflow node list into Create Workflow and Manage Workflows node cards so condition branch target dropdowns can calculate forward branch options safely.
- No DB migration, seed, or executor behavior change required.

## Phase 10.29 - Condition Branch Edges v1
- Added optional true/false branch target fields to CONDITION node parameters in Create Workflow and Manage Workflows.
- Condition branch targets are forward-only and validated server-side to prevent missing targets, self-targets, and backward loops.
- Workflow graph saves now persist conditional edges using the existing `CONDITIONAL` edge type alongside sequential edges.
- Updated inline and Temporal-backed SkyServer workflow executors to route to selected condition branch targets after evaluation.
- Condition output now records branch label, branch target node key, and branch-taken status for Workflow History/debugging.
- Visual Workflow Graph now surfaces TRUE/FALSE branch badges and inspector rows for branch targets.
- No DB migration or seed required.

## Phase 10.28 - Visual Drag Reorder
- Added drag-and-drop reordering to the Admin-Web visual workflow map on Manage Workflows.
- Visual node blocks can now be dragged onto another block to reorder the sequential execution lane before saving.
- Added Move left / Move right controls in the visual node inspector for keyboard/button-driven reorder.
- Reordering updates the existing editor cards immediately while preserving Save workflow graph as the publish point.
- No DB migration, seed, or executor behavior change required.

## Phase 10.27 - Visual Node Inspector
- Enhanced the Admin-Web visual workflow map with a selected-node inspector panel.
- Inspector shows node key, node type, target/URL, condition expression, wait duration, approval role/timeout, and other behavior details based on node type.
- Added Previous / Next / Jump to editor controls so operators can inspect the visual lane before editing the underlying card.
- Updated Manage Workflows visual selection handling so inspector navigation can select nodes without forcing an editor scroll until requested.
- No DB migration, seed, or executor behavior change required.

## Phase 10.26 - Visual Workflow Designer Foundation
- Added a reusable Admin-Web WorkflowVisualGraph component for read-only sequential workflow visualization.
- Manage Workflows now renders the current editable graph as connected visual node blocks above the existing card editor.
- Visual blocks support TOOL, API_CALL, WORKFLOW, TEMPORAL_WORKFLOW, CONDITION, WAIT, and HUMAN_APPROVAL summaries.
- Clicking a visual node scrolls to and highlights the matching editor card so the visual map can drive inspection without replacing the stable save controls.
- No DB migration, seed, or executor behavior change required.

## Phase 10.25.2 - Human Approval Manage Workflow Render Hotfix
- Fixed Admin-Web Manage Workflows blank screen when opening a workflow definition containing a `HUMAN_APPROVAL` node.
- Passed DB-backed approval role targets into workflow node cards in both Manage Workflows and Create Workflow.
- Keeps the Human Approval role dropdown available when editing existing approval nodes after the 10.25.1 role hotfix.

## Phase 10.25 - Human Approval Workflow Nodes
- Added `HUMAN_APPROVAL` as a supported SkyServer workflow node type for durable operator checkpoints.
