Detailed phase notes and implementation history for SkyServer. This file keeps the root README focused on product positioning, architecture, local development, and roadmap status.

## 2026-06-27 — README Roadmap and Documentation Cleanup

- Marked roadmap Phase 9, SkyWeb integration for public-facing macro, as complete.
- Refocused the README around SkyServer's current role as the private Node.js / Express / PostgreSQL control plane for the Sky ecosystem.
- Aligned README structure with SkyWeb's documentation style: stack summary, current status, architecture, local development, repository layout, documentation, and roadmap.
- Moved detailed phase notes and historical implementation entries out of the README and into this `change.log` file.
- Kept Temporal workflow orchestration as the next planned major component while preserving the current worker/tool infrastructure.

## Completed Phase Summary

### Phase 7 — API, Macro, Ingestion Status, and Admin Control Surfaces

- Added macro API endpoints for curated macro views, latest rows, column metadata, indicator registry access, raw indicator series, and macro summary reporting.
- Added full-history macro row payload support for SkyWeb detail pages via `all=true` / `limit=all`, while preserving paginated defaults.
- Added dashboard item support so SkyWeb user dashboard items can reference direct macro indicators as well as saved macro views.
- Added SkyWeb alert-rule backend foundation with user-owned macro alert rules, alert events, and protected alert CRUD/evaluation APIs.
- Added ingestion status endpoints for source health, recent ingestion executions, indicator freshness, stale-data detection, missing-table detection, and per-indicator diagnostics.
- Added admin action endpoints for users, roles, privileges, assignments, sessions, password resets, and read-only system settings.
- Added Admin-Web access control pages for Users, Roles, and Privileges.
- Added Admin-Web ingestion status page for pipeline health, source cards, recent ingestion runs, indicator freshness, and indicator detail inspection.
- Added Dashboard v2 as a command-center view for API/DB health, ingestion status, macro summary, tools, sessions, script executions, audit events, and operator permissions.

### Phase 8 — Worker Automation Foundation

- Added PostgreSQL worker schema and tables for worker nodes, schedules, schedule runs, listeners, and listener events.
- Added standalone worker daemon under `apps/worker` with node registration, heartbeat tracking, schedule polling, due-schedule claiming, scheduled tool execution, and worker-launched script execution logging.
- Added worker-visible tool execution using the relational `core` tool manifest and `worker` visibility channel.
- Added one-time and recurring interval scheduler support.
- Added queue/unqueue controls for immediate schedule execution requests and cancellation of pending requests.
- Added safe schedule archive/delete behavior that removes completed or archived schedules from active views while preserving run history.
- Added worker API endpoints for health, tools, nodes, schedules, runs, listeners, and listener events.
- Added Admin-Web Automation section with Scheduler and Listener pages.
- Added Active Schedules and Active Listeners surfaces.
- Added dashboard automation visibility for worker status, online nodes, active schedules, upcoming run time, and recent automation runs.
- Listener runtime processors remain staged for a later focused implementation; schema, API, and Admin-Web surfaces exist.

### Phase 8.1+ — SkyWeb Alert Rule Foundation

- Added `skyweb` schema support for durable alert rules and evaluation events.
- Added SkyWeb alert endpoints:

```text
GET    /api/skyweb/alerts
POST   /api/skyweb/alerts
GET    /api/skyweb/alerts/:alertKey
PATCH  /api/skyweb/alerts/:alertKey
DELETE /api/skyweb/alerts/:alertKey
POST   /api/skyweb/alerts/:alertKey/evaluate
POST   /api/skyweb/alerts/evaluate
GET    /api/skyweb/alert-preferences
PATCH  /api/skyweb/alert-preferences
GET    /api/skyweb/alert-notifications
PATCH  /api/skyweb/alert-notifications/:notificationId/acknowledge
PATCH  /api/skyweb/alert-notifications/:notificationId/dismiss
POST   /api/skyweb/alert-notifications/acknowledge-all
POST   /api/skyweb/alert-notifications/dismiss-all
```

- Supported condition types: `above`, `below`, `crosses_above`, `crosses_below`, `changes_by`, and `percent_changes_by`.
- Wired scheduled evaluation into the worker scheduler.
- Added triggered SkyWeb alert notifications that can be acknowledged or dismissed while preserving evaluation history.
- Added alert delivery preferences in `skyweb.user_preferences` for in-app surfacing, minimum severity, severity lanes, delivery-mode staging, quiet-hours staging, and future email/browser toggles.
- Added bulk open-signal acknowledgement and dismissal support for Signal Center workflows.

### Phase 9 — SkyWeb Integration for Public-Facing Macro

Phase 9 is complete. SkyServer now supports the public/member-facing SkyWeb Analytics layer while keeping operational execution in SkyServer.

- Added authenticated `/api/skyweb/profile` support for `SKYWEB` app sessions.
- Seeded initial SkyWeb roles, permissions, app memberships, profiles, and preference tables.
- Added authenticated dashboard-preference endpoints:

```text
GET   /api/skyweb/preferences
PATCH /api/skyweb/preferences
```

- Added `skyweb.user_preferences` support for `dashboard_defaults`, including default macro region, macro category, chart period, dashboard density, and preferred landing page.
- Added dedicated `SKYWEB_PREFERENCES_READ` and `SKYWEB_PREFERENCES_WRITE` permissions with compatibility fallbacks for local development.
- Added preference compatibility for `roomy`, `/saved`, `/dashboard`, and `/dashboards` landing behavior as SkyWeb route surfaces evolved.
- Updated `SKYWEB` application seed title to **SkyWeb Analytics** while preserving the app code and permission model.
- Added saved macro view endpoints:

```text
GET    /api/skyweb/saved-views
POST   /api/skyweb/saved-views
PATCH  /api/skyweb/saved-views/:viewKey
DELETE /api/skyweb/saved-views/:viewKey
```

- Stored saved macro views in `skyweb.saved_macro_views` and exposed them through `skyweb.vw_saved_macro_views`.
- Validated saved view keys against the macro view registry and enriched saved records with macro view metadata.
- Added user-owned dashboard endpoints:

```text
GET    /api/skyweb/dashboards
POST   /api/skyweb/dashboards
GET    /api/skyweb/dashboards/:dashboardKey
PATCH  /api/skyweb/dashboards/:dashboardKey
DELETE /api/skyweb/dashboards/:dashboardKey
POST   /api/skyweb/dashboards/:dashboardKey/items
PATCH  /api/skyweb/dashboards/:dashboardKey/items/:itemId
DELETE /api/skyweb/dashboards/:dashboardKey/items/:itemId
```

- Stored dashboard definitions in `skyweb.user_dashboards` and dashboard items in `skyweb.user_dashboard_items`.
- Exposed dashboard read models through `skyweb.vw_user_dashboards` and `skyweb.vw_user_dashboard_items`.
- Added dashboard item metadata for title, note, layout mode, display order, and size.
- Added expanded dashboard item visualization mode compatibility:
  - `view_card`
  - `wide_card`
  - `compact_card`
  - `metric_card`
  - `mini_chart`
  - `latest_row`
  - `table_preview`
- Aligned dashboard item API validation and the `skyweb.user_dashboard_items` check constraint through idempotent migrations.
- Added alert-rule event history access with `GET /api/skyweb/alerts/:alertKey/events` so SkyWeb can inspect the evaluation trail behind each macro alert.
- Added `skyweb_alerts_evaluate` worker tool for scheduled SkyWeb Analytics macro alert checks.
- Added `packages/skyweb/src/evaluateSkyWebAlerts.js` to evaluate active alert rules across users and write `skyweb.alert_rule_events` history.
- Added seed `00030__skyweb_alert_worker_seed.sql` to register the alert evaluator tool, worker visibility, parameters, and a default hourly worker schedule.
- Added `event_metadata.evaluationSource` for distinguishing manual and worker-scheduled evaluations.

## Current Intentional Split

SkyServer continues to own:

- ingestion
- worker automation
- scheduler/listener infrastructure
- repository tooling
- private Admin-Web operations
- alert evaluation execution
- future Temporal orchestration

SkyWeb Analytics owns:

- public/member-facing analytics UI
- ASP.NET Core/C# analytics API
- dashboards and saved views
- chart presentation and alert overlays
- Signal Center and member alert lifecycle presentation

## Phase 10.1 — Temporal Orchestration Foundation

- Added the initial Temporal SDK wiring to SkyServer as a side-by-side workflow lane.
- Added local Temporal configuration helpers under `packages/temporal/src/config.js`.
- Added a Temporal worker entry point under `packages/temporal/src/worker.js`.
- Added a Temporal connectivity check command under `packages/temporal/src/temporalHealth.js`.
- Added the first workflow pilot, `fredIngestionWorkflow`, under `packages/temporal/src/workflows/`.
- Added the first activity wrapper, `loadFredMacroDataActivity`, under `packages/temporal/src/activities/`.
- Wrapped the existing `packages/ingestion/src/loadFREDMacroData.js` script through a child-process activity instead of refactoring ingestion internals immediately.
- Added `npm run temporal:worker`, `temporal:worker:dev`, `temporal:health`, and `temporal:fred` scripts.
- Added Temporal environment placeholders to `.env.example`.
- Added Temporal docs for local setup, FRED pilot validation, and Phase 10 rollout planning.
- Updated README to mark Phase 10 as in progress and document the first Temporal pilot without removing the existing worker/scheduler infrastructure.

## Phase 10.2 — Temporal FRED Indicator-Level Orchestration

- Promoted the FRED Temporal pilot from one child-process script wrapper into indicator-level workflow orchestration.
- Added `listFredIndicatorsActivity` to resolve the full FRED indicator set or an explicit selected subset.
- Added `loadFredIndicatorActivity` to download, normalize, and load one FRED indicator per Temporal Activity.
- Added workflow-level batching with configurable concurrency, defaulting to `3` and capped at `10`.
- Updated the manual FRED runner to support `--indicators`, repeated `--indicator`, `--concurrency`, and `--json`.
- Kept the legacy full-script activity exported for compatibility while moving the active workflow path to structured per-indicator results.

## Phase 10.3 — Temporal Core/API Control Plane

- Added protected SkyServer API routes under `/api/temporal` for Temporal health, workflow definitions, workflow listing, workflow detail, FRED workflow start, workflow cancellation, and workflow termination.
- Added `apps/api/src/services/temporalService.js` as the API-side Temporal client/gateway layer.
- Added `apps/api/src/controllers/temporalController.js` and `apps/api/src/routes/temporal.routes.js`.
- Wired Temporal routes into the SkyServer API server.
- Added approved workflow template metadata for `fredIngestionWorkflow` so future Admin-Web controls can render safe configuration options.
